/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341109/field-2/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5" :answer/id #uuid "bb0a78b3-8824-5702-8be4-655150ec42cb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\ge 0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341109/field-2/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" :answer/id #uuid "06173a57-b1d0-525d-ab3d-44059927cf60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s>0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341109/field-2/ef9beb211f655a6c04dcd4fe42de854d9485336754f46d6dec47ec7e8aed6b34" :answer/id #uuid "3c04c114-e641-5762-8cd0-b9fb5a400617" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "s\\ge -4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341109/field-2" :answer-field/id #uuid "242e250f-971a-56fd-92a2-c9094eb117f4" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341109/field-2/23424e5dffaca1bffc81dd2cc015a958b04177158815d98fdd41149314b3d874" :answer-field/choices ["q-341109/field-2/89cc92a5a256d32ea65399b5196bd1fc92b2d3f166799d13cfa09c67368e2d16" "q-341109/field-2/23424e5dffaca1bffc81dd2cc015a958b04177158815d98fdd41149314b3d874" "q-341109/field-2/34021d3854d8d25832b91720cc624a8e35c2f6fd4d7bab524d021edef59e6673" "q-341109/field-2/9d34e85dabb5082358af9360d93c7ce717fcea0db3670310b8eab46db4fc35b5" "q-341109/field-2/de63348529d477cd70740ab9581d04b231678372657a4ecc21dd12e21b5d033c" "q-341109/field-2/ef9beb211f655a6c04dcd4fe42de854d9485336754f46d6dec47ec7e8aed6b34"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-341109" :question/id #uuid "1463b6de-f11a-5f9e-b1d5-6cc54aaacf1a" :question/math-academy-id "q-341109" :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{kt}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that, by definition\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)=\\frac{{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-4t}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4t}+{e}^{-4t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4t}}{2}+\\frac{{e}^{-4t}}{2}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{4t}}{2}}+L{\\frac{{e}^{-4t}}{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{4t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-4t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{kt}}=\\frac{1}{s-k},\\,s>k.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-4},\\,s>4 \\\\ L{{e}^{-4t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+4},\\,s>-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)} & =\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{4t}}+\\frac{1}{2}L{{e}^{-4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{1}{s-4}+\\frac{1}{s+4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{(s+4)+(s-4)}{(s-4)(s+4)}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\frac{2s}{{s}^{2}-16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, since $L{{e}^{4t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (4,\\infty )$ and $L{{e}^{-4t}}$ is defined for $s\\in (-4,\\infty ),$ we have that $L{\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4t)}$ is defined for\n\n$$\n(4,\\infty )\\cap (-4,\\infty )=(4,\\infty ),\n$$\n\nthat is, $s>4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-341109/field-1" "q-341109/field-2"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c086bc97-415d-52c9-b26a-02dc8aebef33"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-341109"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144314 :answer-field/correct 17592186144316 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id 17592186144307 :answer-field/correct 17592186144311 :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-340665"] :question/problem "Use the Laplace transform of $f(t)={e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}$ to find the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t).$$\\,L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)}=$ {{field-1}},\ndefined for {{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "The linearity property of the Laplace transform states that for functions $f(t)$ and $g(t),$ we have\n\n$$\nL{\\alpha f(t)+\\beta g(t)}=\\alpha \\cdot L{f(t)}+\\beta \\cdot L{g(t)},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\alpha $ and $\\beta $ are constants.\n\nFirst, recall that the sine function can be defined in terms of complex exponentials as follows: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)=\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}\n$$\n\nTaking the Laplace transform and applying the linearity property, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)} & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}-{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}-\\frac{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =L{\\frac{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}}-L{\\frac{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}{2\\text{i}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we recall that \n\n$$\nL{{e}^{\\text{i}\\omega t}}=\\frac{1}{s-\\text{i}\\omega },\\,s>0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s-3\\text{i}},\\,s>0 \\\\ L{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}} & =\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}},\\,s>0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3t)} & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{3\\text{i}t}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}L{{e}^{-3\\text{i}t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s-3\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}\\cdot \\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{1}{s-3\\text{i}}-\\frac{1}{s+3\\text{i}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{(s+3\\text{i})-(s-3\\text{i})}{(s-3\\text{i})(s+3\\text{i})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2\\text{i}}(\\frac{6\\text{i}}{{s}^{2}+9}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{{s}^{2}+9},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ndefined for $s>0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-341127/field-1/5905829824aec3466fad250f317062c28ce64f3a237391d18eeddbade06bbc05" :answer/id #uuid "f40ed9b6-feca-56b6-876b-1056bfedd1c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}-144}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341127/field-1/e57fffefd59ac7fb17054fe8c8182dd4a785287834dbfca936296e607065d64c" :answer/id #uuid "c8d3603e-7225-5597-826b-a3e69d083d0f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{s}{{s}^{2}+144}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341127/field-1/1e136a0884cf23323b59d14c2c5f3eee47208a164b4c927fccec1074dba3b3f1" :answer/id #uuid "8a001fa0-bd54-53ff-8b8c-7c0a7a8f67ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12s}{{s}^{2}+144}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341127/field-1/44ffc3bc7c7ade1b4581ca9b34dc4e50732bc0ee769e1bb662562d445f617e32" :answer/id #uuid "68a74458-1174-567d-99e3-ab6ef44838e9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}+144}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341127/field-1/03a411fa30e1a4d555cc65b43a7e38281ae2fc78cf70bf0e4ffc05153f94580e" :answer/id #uuid "78627af5-1bf5-527a-a740-e124f37b8ea3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{12}{{s}^{2}-144}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-341127/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "de0f1d1b-73ae-588e-96ae-a02e338d5afd" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/select :answer-field/correct "q-341127/field-1/44ffc3bc7c7ade1b4581ca9b34dc4e50732bc0ee769e1bb662562d445f617e32" :answer-field/choices ["q-341127/field-1/5905829824aec3466fad250f317062c28ce64f3a237391d18eeddbade06bbc05" "q-341127/field-1/e57fffefd59ac7fb17054fe8c8182dd4a785287834dbfca936296e607065d64c" "q-341127/field-1/1e136a0884cf23323b59d14c2c5